From f392f36e01ec1ffd8c0b8de99608c909beca9e3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:32:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(mobile): deliver keys held with Ctrl, Alt or Meta as
 shortcuts
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On a phone or tablet with a hardware keyboard the modifiers never reached the
widgets. Android left them unset ("TODO(crawshaw): set Modifiers") and
typeDownCanvas ignored them except for Tab, so Ctrl+Up arrived as a plain Up
and Ctrl+C as C: a chat that edits your last message on Up did it on Ctrl+Up
too.

- Android reads the meta state of each key event (keyModifiers).
- typeDownCanvas delivers a key held with Control, Alt or Meta as a shortcut,
  as the desktop driver does: Control (Command on iOS) with Z, Y, V, C, X or A
  is the standard shortcut, anything else a desktop.CustomShortcut, to the
  focused Shortcutable or else to the canvas. A key that still produces a
  character with Alt alone is typed: AltGr, which Android reports as Alt,
  writes "@" or "€" on many European layouts.
- Android no longer also hands those keys to the hidden EditText behind the
  soft keyboard, which applied Ctrl+V to it and would paste twice.

Tested: TestTypeDownCanvas_ModifiersMakeShortcuts and
TestTypeDownCanvas_ShortcutWithoutFocusGoesToTheCanvas (red without the
typeDownCanvas change), TestKeyModifiers and TestKeyIsShortcut.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K7a9FPvLA4FsHbm41nkUrM
